<title>USA: GOLF-FINAL SCORES FROM BAY HILL INVITATIONAL.</title>
<headline>GOLF-FINAL SCORES FROM BAY HILL INVITATIONAL.</headline>
<dateline>ORLANDO, Florida 1997-03-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Final scores from the $1.5 million Bay Hill Invitational PGA golf tournament won by Phil Mickelson on Sunday (U.S. unless noted):</p>
<p>272 Phil Mickelson 72 65 70 65</p>
<p>275 Stuart Appleby (Australia) 73 63 70 69</p>
<p>276 Payne Stewart 69 70 70 67, Mark O'Meara 72 66 68 70, Omar Uresti 69 67 69 71</p>
<p>277 Michael Bradley 71 69 69 68, Loren Roberts 70 67 70 70, Tim Herron 70 70 66 71</p>
<p>278 Tiger Woods 68 71 71 68, Davis Love 73 68 67 70</p>
<p>279 Brian Henninger 70 68 73 68, Nick Price (Zimbabwe) 70 68</p>
<p>73 68, Robert Damron 70 70 69 70</p>
<p>280 Mark Calcavecchia 71 70 72 67, Paul Stankowski 67 70 74</p>
<p>69, Doug Martin 71 68 71 70, John Morse 71 69 70 70, Chris Perry 69 71 68 72</p>
<p>281 Jay Don Blake 69 70 74 68, Jeff Maggert 70 69 74 68, Colin Montgomerie (Britain) 73 66 70 72</p>
<p>Add non-U.S. scores:</p>
<p>282 Bernhard Langer (Germany) 69 70 72 71</p>
<p>283 Craig Parry (Australia) 72 70 69 72</p>
<p>284 Vijay Singh (Fiji) 69 72 71 72</p>
<p>287 Ian Woosnam (Britain) 70 73 76 68</p>
<p>288 Naomichi &quot;Joe&quot; Ozaki 70 73 74 71</p>
<p>289 Nick Faldo (Britain) 71 70 73 75</p>
<p>290 Grant Waite (New Zealand) 71 73 74 72</p>
<p>300 Wayne Grady (Australia) 72 71 76 81</p>
